  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1227 PM CST Fri Nov 20 2026\n\nLow clouds remain in place over much of the region from the Missouri \nvalley east into west central MN early this afternoon. There is some \nerosion from southwest to northeast into the James valley, but so \nfar any gaps have filled back in relatively quickly. The clouds and \ndrizzle are suppressing daytime highs in the warm sector. A cold \nfront moves through this evening with a deep upper low behind it \nthat will drag in significantly colder air through the day Saturday. \nThere could be a non-diurnal spread especially as clouds move back \nin with the front tonight and the caa spreads southeast through 21z \nSat. Behind it all on Sunday, expect highs only in the 30s which is \naround or slightly below climo norms for late November. \n\nStrong high pressure builds in on Tuesday. The colder temperatures \nand mostly dry conditions will persist from Saturday through the \nmiddle of next week. There's the potential for a ridge to build in \naloft on Thanksgiving along with southerly sfc flow ahead of the \nnext front. Those two features could see highs pop back into the 40s \nfor Thursday and Friday.",
